WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.800
- I hear that your mom has been sitting in

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.633
on your interviews.

00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:03.466
Is that right?

00:00:03.466 --> 00:00:04.299
Because you're 14, right?

00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:05.132
- [Malia] That is correct.

00:00:05.132 --> 00:00:05.965
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:05.965 --> 00:00:06.810
Is that good? Because I think-

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.920
- You know, there are some good instances

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.680
and there are some bad
aspects of it, you know?

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.250
Like, texting in the middle of practice,

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.380
"Fix your face right now, Malia.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.970
Just, like, smile a little bit more,"

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.490
and I'm like, "Okay, that's comforting.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:19.323
Awesome really, really cool."

00:00:19.323 --> 00:00:20.910
- Just so you know, I'm 39,

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.870
and my mom literally just texted me,

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:24.370
like, tips for me and Blake.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.400
We're being too mean to
each other on The Voice.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.460
Yeah, yeah, she reprimands me at 39.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.549
So, this isn't changing.

00:00:29.549 --> 00:00:30.573
- Oh, this is comforting. This is great.

00:00:30.573 --> 00:00:32.860
- [Kelly] So just lean in, lean in...

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.290
- Lean in to it? Got it. Okay.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.117
- So, does your mom, your
mom is here today, right?

00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:36.994
- She is here.

00:00:36.994 --> 00:00:38.157
- [Kelly] Your mom is
here? Is she right here?

00:00:38.157 --> 00:00:38.990
- She is here. Oh, she's waving.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.215
- [Kelly] What's up mama?

00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:41.920
(audience applauding )

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.605
- So how is she doing so far, mom?

00:00:43.605 --> 00:00:47.770
- Well, I mean, she's here,
so the text obviously works

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.453
and I'm just in awe.

00:00:49.453 --> 00:00:50.424
(laughs)

00:00:50.424 --> 00:00:52.962
- [Kelly] Exactly, it's
working, the plan is working.

00:00:52.962 --> 00:00:53.795
- Totally.

00:00:53.795 --> 00:00:56.170
- Um, so, Malia, was your
mom always encouraging

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:57.610
of your acting or was she a little scared?

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.160
Because as a mama, I
would be a little scared.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:00:59.993
- [Malia] Yeah, for sure.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.650
I mean, there's always gonna
be those doubts, kind of,

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:02.960
and those fears in the back of you mind.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.630
There's insecurities as well,

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.670
but she was really
supporting from the start.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:08.430
You know, my family has
being my biggest supporter,

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:09.930
which I feel like getting
into this industry

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.220
is the one thing that you need.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.053
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:01:12.053 --> 00:01:14.232
- But she gave me one year to the date

00:01:14.232 --> 00:01:16.980
of, you know, being able
to drive to the city,

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:17.830
because I live on a farm.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.010
So, drive to the city,

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.640
which is like an hour plus away

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.790
and do auditions and
if it didn't work out,

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:23.623
then it didn't work out,

00:01:23.623 --> 00:01:24.590
and I was understanding of that.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:25.940
But a year to the date,

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.300
I picked up Babysitter's
Club and here I am.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.133
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:29.966
- Yeah.

00:01:29.966 --> 00:01:30.799
(audience applauds)

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:31.733
- On Netflix! That's amazing.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.950
- [Kelly] So, wait. Now you're
on the Babysitter's Club.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.230
Way to go for that year deal.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.517
That worked out.

00:01:38.517 --> 00:01:40.210
So, does your character deal with,

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.910
like, a lot of the same things
that you feel like you deal

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:42.743
with in your life?

00:01:42.743 --> 00:01:45.300
- Yeah, I mean, there's that
kinda like teen awkwardness

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.190
that we both go through.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:47.770
I mean, I always joke about we practically

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:49.380
went through puberty on Netflix

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.250
and I feel like that's very-

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.083
- That's rough.

00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:53.590
- It was rough, you know, with everything.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.700
So figuring out how to
navigate friends, and school

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.580
and social life,

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.300
and I had my first kiss
on the series as well, so-

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.133
- [Kelly] What?

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.061
- [Malia] Yeah!

00:02:02.061 --> 00:02:04.880
- [Kelly] Wait, your
first kiss was at work?

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.040
- With all the producers
that flew down from LA

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.120
for that specific scene,

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.504
so yes, that was interesting.

00:02:11.504 --> 00:02:12.760
- Oh, my gosh! People were watching?

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:13.593
That's weird.

00:02:13.593 --> 00:02:14.958
Your first kiss.

00:02:14.958 --> 00:02:15.791
My first kiss was horrible though.

00:02:15.791 --> 00:02:16.624
So, you know?

00:02:16.624 --> 00:02:17.900
- [Hasan] Malia, you are so brave.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.309
You're talking about this in front of mom.

00:02:19.309 --> 00:02:20.534
(audience laughs)

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:23.137
- [Malia] She was
videotaping the whole thing!

00:02:25.838 --> 00:02:27.053
- This is bad parenting.

00:02:27.053 --> 00:02:27.886
- Thank you!

00:02:27.886 --> 00:02:29.272
(audience laughs)

00:02:29.272 --> 00:02:30.710
- You need to be like Indian parents.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:31.610
We don't talk about it.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.070
The first time I kissed

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.850
was when Beena and I got married.

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.769
(audience laughs)

00:02:36.769 --> 00:02:39.040
- [Hasan] The way God intended, mom.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.710
We didn't just kiss for
SAG after residuals.

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:42.552
Do you understand?

00:02:42.552 --> 00:02:43.746
(audience laughs)

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:46.820
- We kissed for something
deeper, like love.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.300
- No, you can't count that though

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.080
because I did have, like, a stage kiss

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.280
in musical theater growing up.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.830
I didn't count that as
like a first, you know.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:54.690
- True, exactly, you know?

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:55.778
- It counts.

00:02:55.778 --> 00:02:56.696
- [Kelly] No!

00:02:56.696 --> 00:02:57.529
- Malia, it counts.

00:02:57.529 --> 00:02:58.362
- No.

00:02:58.362 --> 00:02:59.458
- All right guys, we're
not gonna have a debate

00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:00.291
about this now.

00:03:00.291 --> 00:03:01.720
- I just call that homework
until the real thing happens.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.690
The real test happens.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.090
- Its a little like test, for sure,

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.380
and then the fourth and the fifth,

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.180
and then many takes of that happens.

